================================================================================
TRANSFORM: Fix descending range labels to ascending (lines 47-50)
================================================================================

FIND (exact):
```javascript
      var from = Math.min(s.from, total);
      var label = s.label || (fmt(from) + '\u2013' + fmt(s.to) + ' months');
      if (!s.label && s.from === 24) label = (total >= 12 ? fmt(total) : fmt(from)) + '\u201312 months';
```

REPLACE WITH:
```javascript
      var from = Math.min(s.from, total);
      var lo = Math.min(from, s.to), hi = Math.max(from, s.to);
      var label = s.label || (fmt(lo) + '\u2013' + fmt(hi) + ' months');
      if (!s.label && s.from === 24) label = (total >= 12 ? '12' : fmt(lo)) + '+ months';
```

================================================================================
EXPLANATION
================================================================================

BEFORE (BUG):
  - Stage {from: 24, to: 12} → label "24–12 months" (DESCENDING)
  - Stage {from: 12, to: 9}  → label "12–9 months"  (DESCENDING)
  
AFTER (FIX):
  - Stage {from: 24, to: 12} → label "12+ months"   (matches static HTML)
  - Stage {from: 12, to: 9}  → label "9–12 months"  (ASCENDING)
  - Stage {from: 9, to: 6}   → label "6–9 months"   (ASCENDING)
  - etc.

PRESERVED:
  - Stage list order (farther-from-wedding first)
  - Special labels: "Final month", "Wedding week"
  - Date window meaning (stages still cover same time periods)
  - Currency/locale formatting (not applicable here)

